\par See \ref{restatable:convergencetv}
\@proof Recall that
$$\lim_{t\to\infty}D(q_{n},\tilde{\nu}^{\pi}_{n}\mid\tilde{h}^{\lx@scalerel@obj{(n)}}_{&lt;t})=0,\quad\tilde{\nu}^{\pi}_{n}\text{-a.s.}$$
In other words, there exists an event $\tilde{S}_{n}\subseteq\tilde{\Omega}^{\lx@scalerel@obj{(n)}}$, with $\tilde{\nu}^{\pi}_{n}(\tilde{S}_{n})=1$, where $D(q_{n},\tilde{\nu}^{\pi}_{n}\mid\tilde{h}^{\lx@scalerel@obj{(n)}}_{&lt;t})$ converges to $0$ pointwise.
Let $F$ be the set of ``faulty'' outcomes in $\tilde{S}_{n}$ whose augmented returns $\tilde{z}_{i\equiv n}$ do not agree with the true returns $z_{i\equiv n}$.
Recall the definition of $\tilde{\nu}^{\pi}_{n}$ as the pushforward of $\nu^{\pi}$ by $\aug_n$.Since$F$isdisjointfromtheimageof$\aug_n$,weget$\tilde{\nu}^\pi_n (F)=0$.\par Let$S_n$bethepreimageof${\tilde{S}_n} - F$under$\aug_n$.Then,bytheinjectivityof$\aug_n$,weseethat$\nu^\pi(S_n) = \tilde{\nu}^\pi_n(\tilde{S}_n - F) = \tilde{\nu}^\pi_n (\tilde{S}_n)=1$.Sincepointwiseconvergenceon$\tilde{S}_n$impliespointwiseconvergenceonthesubset$\tilde{S}_n - F$,weseethat$D(q_n, \tilde{\nu}^\pi_n \mid{{\aug_n}(h)}_{&lt;t})$convergespointwiseto$0$on$S_n$.Constructsuch$S_n$forevery$n$,andlet$S = \bigcap_n S_n$.Then,$\nu^\pi(S) =1$,and$D(q_n, \tilde{\nu}^\pi_n \mid{{\aug_n}(h)}_{&lt;t})$convergespointwiseto$0$on$S$forall$n$.\qed\end@proof\par\par\par\par See\ref{restatable:errorreturnpredictor}\@proof Fixsome$\beta&gt;0$.By\lx@cref{creftype~refnum}{thm:convergence_tv},wecanchoosesome$S\subseteq\Omega$with$\nu^{\pi}(S)=1$suchthat$\forall h\in S$,$\exists t_{0},\forall t\geq t_{0},\forall n\in[0,N-1]$,\begin{equation}D(q_{n},\tilde{\nu}^{\pi}_{n}\mid{{\aug{}_{n}}(h)}_{&lt;t}) &lt; \beta.
\end{equation}
Consider some $h\in S$ and $t\geq t_{0}$. For all $m\in[t,t{+}N{-}H]$ and $n=m\,\mathrm{mod}\,N$, we see that \lx@cref{creftype~refnum}{eq:condition_aug} is satisfied for both $t$ and $m$, so we can apply $\aug{}_{n}$onhistoriesoflengths$t-1$and$m-1$.Then,forafixed$a'_{m} \in\mathcal{A}$,\begin{aligned} &amp;\hskip 11.0pt\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}h^{\prime}_{&lt;m}\in\mathcal{T},\\
\tilde{z}_{m}\in\mathcal{Z}\end{subarray}}\nu^{\pi}\left(h^{\prime}_{t:m-1}a^{\prime}_{m}\mid h_{&lt;t}\right)\cdot\big|\psi(\tilde{z}_{m}\mid h^{\prime}_{&lt;m}a^{\prime}_{m})-\nu^{\pi}(\tilde{z}_{m}\mid h^{\prime}_{&lt;m}a^{\prime}_{m})\big|\\
&amp;\end{aligned}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
